iginally reaching the Atlantic Ocean (Bay of Biscay), between present-day Spain and France.\nThe medieval state took form around the city of Pamplona during the first centuries of the Iberian Reconquista. The kingdom had its origins in the conflict in the buffer region between the Carolingian Empire and the Umayyad Emirate of Córdoba that controlled most of the Iberian Peninsula. The city of Pamplona (Latin: Pompaelo; Basque: Iruña), had been the main city of the indigenous Vasconic population and was located in a predominantly Basque-speaking area."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q10282","value_label":"Pamplona","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Pamplona"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q397","value_label":"Latin","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Latin"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q14185","value_label":"Occitan","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Occitan"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q1321","value_label":"Spanish","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Spanish"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q8752","value_label":"Basque","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Basque"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q8752","value_label":"Basque","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Basque"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q1321","value_label":"Spanish","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Spanish"},{"qid":"Q200262","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q8765","value_label":"Aragonese","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","v